# Phase 6 spike on the SECOND physical device.
#
# Xiaomi 25010PN30C (xuanyuan), Android 15 / API 35, SM8550, arm64-v8a, 5 cameras,
# 4 KB pages, HyperOS OS2.0.207.0.VOACNXM, rooted with Magisk.
#
# Reached through a private root-agent control channel, not adb: no ADB listener is
# opened on this phone. Same protocol as tools/maint/camera-spike-run.sh -- cold start, force-stop, 2 s
# for the HAL to release, logcat streamed to a file, 15 runs, median reported. Every flavor
# in this set was asked for, and got, a 1920x1080 frame.
#
# Two things this device needs that DN-ENG41 does not, both found by watching it fail:
#   - "svc power stayon true". The screen times out partway through a 15-run loop and the
#     paused activity stops receiving frames, which reads exactly like a backend failure.
#   - "cmd appops set <pkg> CAMERA allow" as well as "pm grant". HyperOS revokes the
#     runtime grant again after an app opens the camera without a user-visible prompt;
#     "dumpsys package" then says granted=false and appops says "Uid mode: ignore", while
#     CameraX logs "cannot open camera 0 without camera permission" in a 700 ms retry loop
#     forever. Fifteen runs reported no result at all before this was understood.
#
device: 25010PN30C, sdk 35
fingerprint: Xiaomi/xuanyuan/xuanyuan:15/AQ3A.240912.001/OS2.0.207.0.VOACNXM:user/release-keys
package: io.github.kakakakacat.zxing.spike.cameraxlean, runs: 15, backCameraOnly=1

